# Build context exclusions for the hub image (deploy/docker/Dockerfile).
# Keep this list tight: the image must build from a clean clone.
#
# PURPOSE (distinct from .gitignore): this file decides what is sent to the Docker
# daemon as the build context. Anything here is still in the working tree and still
# in git's view - it just never reaches an image layer. Secrets must be excluded
# here as well as in .gitignore, because a key that is not committed can still end
# up baked into a layer.

# --- build trees (large, host-specific, contain downloaded deps) ---
hg_build/
hg_asan/
hg_asan_e/
hg_asan_f1/
hg_asan_f21/
hg_verify/
hg_f1_verify/
hg_f21_verify/
hg_android/
hg_android27/
hg_apk_build/
hg_asan_f22/
hg_asan_f22b/
build/
build_final/
apk/
cmake-build-*/

# --- VCS + editors ---
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- untracked local material that must never enter an image ---
example/
node_modules/

# --- runtime artefacts: databases, WAL/SHM sidecars, logs, credentials ---
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.log
homeguardian.log
deploy/docker/secrets/creds.json

# --- D-03 certificate material and device credentials (NEVER in a layer) ---
# The ingress reads certificates from a READ-ONLY bind mount at run time. Baking
# them in would put a private key in an image layer, where it survives in docker
# history and in every copy of the image, and make rotation a rebuild.
deploy/docker/certs/
certs/
**/certs/
# Private keys and certificate material of EVERY kind, at ANY depth. The `**/`
# prefix is not decoration: `*.key` matches only at the context root in Docker's
# matcher, so a key one directory down leaked into the context (this was caught by
# building a probe image and looking for the file, not by reading the rules).
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.crt
**/*.cer
**/*.csr
**/*.srl
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.keytab
# Provisioned device credentials and operator registries: these carry credential
# fingerprints and consent records, which identify real devices.
**/devices.json
**/devices.*.json
**/revocations.json
**/revocations.*.json
**/ca.srl
# Locally generated secrets and temporary credential/provisioning directories.
**/*.secret
**/*.secrets
**/*.secret.json
**/secrets/
**/.secrets/
**/credentials/
**/private/
**/tmp-certs/
**/tmp_creds/
**/provisioned/

# --- misc ---
**/*.swp
.DS_Store
